WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.588
Follow the product-contact path through
the fictional vessel.

2
00:00:03.708 --> 00:00:06.567
Include the agitator, gaskets, valve seats

3
00:00:06.687 --> 00:00:09.674
and transfer connection, not only the
metal shell.

4
00:00:09.794 --> 00:00:11.794
The installation check asks

5
00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:15.455
whether the specified materials are
actually represented

6
00:00:15.575 --> 00:00:18.348
by the installed components and their
evidence.

7
00:00:18.468 --> 00:00:20.730
A certificate for the vessel body does

8
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.751
not identify an elastomer fitted later.

9
00:00:24.371 --> 00:00:26.995
A certificate says material grade X, but

10
00:00:27.115 --> 00:00:29.440
which installed item does it describe?

11
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.672
Use the applicable identifiers

12
00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:36.086
and controlled supplier traceability to
link the record to the component.

13
00:00:36.206 --> 00:00:39.769
The precise method depends on the
component and project.

14
00:00:39.889 --> 00:00:43.729
Do not require one universal certificate
format or assume

15
00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:47.412
every gasket has a readable individual
serial number.

16
00:00:47.532 --> 00:00:50.454
Evaluate the traceability actually
available.

17
00:00:51.074 --> 00:00:54.210
In our example, the vessel certificate is
available

18
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.533
but the installed gasket lot cannot be
linked to its material record.

19
00:00:58.653 --> 00:01:00.653
Keep the gasket finding open.

20
00:01:00.773 --> 00:01:03.479
The vessel certificate does not fill that
gap.

21
00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:07.055
Obtain applicable traceability, or use an
authorized

22
00:01:07.175 --> 00:01:10.098
corrective approach followed by
verification.

23
00:01:10.218 --> 00:01:14.612
Changing a label without evidence would
only conceal the uncertainty.

24
00:01:15.232 --> 00:01:18.176
Material identity and material suitability

25
00:01:18.296 --> 00:01:20.430
are related but different questions.

26
00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:24.020
The design review should have considered
intended exposure,

27
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.724
while installation evidence identifies
what was fitted.

28
00:01:27.844 --> 00:01:32.708
If an authorized substitution changes the
material, assess the compatibility

29
00:01:32.828 --> 00:01:36.220
and qualification implications through
change control.

30
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.929
Do not declare cleaning effectiveness
solely

31
00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:42.334
because the installed material matches a
certificate.
